@ [profile] cantor-sjs-commit-envelope-journal/0.1

& [Requirements]
  + [CEJ-001] strict journal link record placement and receipt forms use closed profiles bounded fields and deny unknown machine fields
  + [CEJ-002] a bundle contains 1 through 32 ordered links one anchor one open tip verification_only physical_contact false and a self-excluding digest
  + [CEJ-003] each link embeds one existing P0 DiffInventory candidate manifest candidate receipt published manifest and published receipt
  + [CEJ-004] existing unmodified P0 validators must accept the candidate manifest inventory and candidate receipt
  + [CEJ-005] existing unmodified P0 validators must accept the published manifest same inventory and published receipt
  + [CEJ-006] candidate state is exactly candidate with no resulting commit and published state is exactly published with one resulting commit
  + [CEJ-007] candidate and published typed content is identical after normalizing only publication state resulting commit and change-set digest
  + [CEJ-008] record binds change-set repository branch payload predecessor/result inventory and both manifest and receipt digests
  + [CEJ-009] record journal path is normalized unique per bundle and absent from the payload inventory it describes
  + [CEJ-010] record policy is exactly immediate_successor one-head-lag verification_only physical_contact false with a domain-separated self digest
  + [CEJ-011] supplied placement binds record digest journal path carrier parent and carrier commit under supplied_data physical_contact false
  + [CEJ-012] placement carrier parent equals payload resulting commit and carrier commit differs from the parent
  + [CEJ-013] first payload predecessor equals anchor and final carrier commit equals the sole open tip
  + [CEJ-014] consecutive links require next predecessor equals prior payload result and next result equals prior carrier commit
  + [CEJ-015] deterministic bundle and receipt digests bind exact link count closed payload count one open tip and nonauthority
  + [CEJ-016] CLI reads one bounded bundle JSON and emits one receipt to stdout only with typed first-fault JSON
  + [CEJ-017] tests cover one-link and multi-link success deterministic replay plus all T01 through T18 refusal families
  + [CEJ-018] static and executable evidence prove no Git command process filesystem write network provider model MCP tool mutation or unsafe code
  + [CEJ-019] exact focused debug overflow-checked release workspace Clippy format evidence attribution commit and post-push gates pass
  + [CEJ-020] physical Git placement truth hook staging commit push recovery operator authorization provider activation and self-signature remain absent

& [Constraints]
  + C01 safe Rust only and no new Cargo dependency
  + C02 reuse existing P0 forms validators digests and receipts without modification
  + C03 chain is linear ordered nonempty and at most 32 links
  + C04 repository and branch are equal across bundle links inventories and manifests
  + C05 all commit identities are lowercase forty-hex SHA-1 profile values
  + C06 anchor payload results carriers and open tip cannot collapse into self loops
  + C07 each record change-set UUID equals both manifests and both receipts
  + C08 candidate and published receipts are independently exact P0 receipts
  + C09 graph events exclusions inventory and all nonpublication manifest fields are invariant
  + C10 journal paths use existing normalized repository path rules
  + C11 journal path is absent from its payload inventory coordinate sides
  + C12 journal paths are unique within a bundle
  + C13 placement is explicitly supplied_data and not physical observation
  + C14 authority is verification_only and physical_contact false on all P2 outputs
  + C15 bundle receipt declares one intentionally open tip and no complete-current-tip claim
  + C16 CLI has no output path and writes no file
  + C17 no ambient time randomness environment Git provider or network input
  + C18 no Cargo feature manifest or lockfile delta
  + C19 no foreign unstaged or untracked custody
  + C20 no claim that P2 observes a commit tree or authorizes a broker
  + C21 domain-separated self-excluding digests use deterministic serde JSON
  + C22 typed first faults distinguish profile identity path P0 invariant chain digest authority resource serialization IO and CLI failures

& [ImplementationBoundary]
  + one pure child module one stdout-only CLI unit integration/static fixtures builder evidence solution proof review narrative and publication bookend

& [SignatureState]
  + artifact lock proof review and satisfaction signature required before code
